# What stays out of the .vsix. Same syntax as .gitignore, opposite default:
# `vsce` packages everything not listed here, so without this file the shipped
# extension carries its own source, its ten test harnesses, a captured ACL2
# log and an icon-drawing script -- none of which a reader installs.
#
# What ships is `out/` (package.json's `main`), `media/`, `syntaxes/`, the two
# configuration JSONs, the README and the licence. Everything else is how the
# extension is *built*, which is what a repository is for.

# The sources. `out/` is what runs; shipping `src/` doubles the download to
# no end, and the sourcemaps that point at it are three times the size again.
src/**
out/**/*.js.map
tsconfig.json

# The harnesses, and the corpus fixture one of them reads.
*.mjs
test/**

# Icon-drawing, run by hand when the icon changes.
tools/**

# Build and repository furniture.
.vscode/**
.gitignore
.vscodeignore
node_modules/.bin/**
package-lock.json

# `@vscode/codicons` ships its whole design source -- SVGs, previews, a
# handlebars template. The extension loads exactly one file from it, the
# font that `pageHtml` resolves for the webviews' fold chevrons.
node_modules/@vscode/codicons/**
!node_modules/@vscode/codicons/dist/codicon.ttf
